{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793473539,"nonce":"zsEB+UuI3BmGLWP8iMSbYNm1IU8=","title":"Lua: os.clock reports wall time since its first call, not CPU time","message":"host_clock (crates/zyntax_lua/src/host.rs) returns the time elapsed since the first os.clock call, so `print(os.clock())` at the top of a program prints 0.0 where Lua and LuaJIT print the process's CPU time so far (luajit: 0.003244), and a loop's os.clock difference is wall time. Lua's os.clock is clock()/CLOCKS_PER_SEC, the process's CPU time over all its threads. Changing it moves the benchmark kernels' reported elapsed: process CPU time includes the compile threads' work, which wall time does not count while they run beside the program.","files":null}]}